# Gurobi reads this file automatically from the working directory and applies it
# to EVERY model it creates in the process — the B&S solver, the DECOMP master
# MIQCP, and the OBBT / dispatch LP sub-solves alike.
#
# NLHPC policy: never use more CPU than the Slurm allocation (--cpus-per-task=8).
# Without this, Gurobi defaults to ALL physical cores on the compute node, which
# is what got job 8176372 (ce_pipeline) flagged for over-utilisation: 8 CPUs
# reserved, ~32 threads running (>400% CPU). The `export GRB_THREADS` in the
# slurm scripts is NOT enough — Gurobi does not read that variable; only
# node_obbt_hpc._make_decomp consumes it, and only for the master solve.
#
# Keep this value equal to --cpus-per-task in the slurm scripts.
Threads 8
